mmand in the\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-139-  tests key of its worker role in .ard/config.yaml. Run it as is. Do not\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-140-  substitute a tool of your own choosing (for example go vet alone) when\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-141-  an entry point exists, because it can skip checks such as a format\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-142-  check. Only when the repository names none, fall back to the\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-143-  toolchain's usual linter, vet and format check, and say in ## Checks\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-144-  that there is no repository lint entry point and which tools you used.\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt:145:  When the Trust rule stops you from running the entry point, say so in\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-146-  ## Checks and then use the fallback. Report only problems on lines the\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-147-  change added or in files it changed; ignore problems that were there\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-148-  before.\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-149-- Diff coverage: when the toolchain can report coverage, run the tests of\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-150-  the changed packages or modules with coverage, writing the report to\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-151-  your temporary directory, and find the added lines and new functions\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-152-  that no test executes. A missing test is a finding.\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-153-- When the repository has a test command, the worker's run of it already\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-154-  passed: the controller does not review a pull request whose tests\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-155-  failed. Run targeted commands, not the whole suite again, and work\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-156-  economically, because the job has a time and money budget.\nreviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt-157-- If a check cannot run here (a missing tool, no such command, a network","is_error":false}]},"